  "key_findings": [
    "Break-even ROAS is 2.20 on net revenue and 2.28 as the platforms report it, because they record the order total with tax. A new customer can cost up to 53.17 and still pay back within 6 months; on the first order alone the limit is 20.45.",
    "2 live targets lose money if hit: Meta Prospecting | Broad (cost cap 58.00, bid_amount 5800 cents); TikTok Ads Spark | Value (ROAS bid 0.80).",
    "MER is 3.54 against a break-even of 2.20, leaving 14,546 after ads. Blended CAC is 34.64: above the first-order limit of 20.45 and below the 6-month limit of 53.17, so it pays back within 6 months through repeat orders; a new customer needs 1.69 orders' margin to pay back.",
    "The 3.0 ROAS the founder wants on Meta is out of reach at today's rates: Meta runs at 1.90 (range 1.74 to 2.06), so it needs a 58.2% higher conversion rate or a 36.8% lower CPC. If it were hit, its verdict would be 'clears the profit goal'.",
    "Making 60,000 from ads takes about 1,333 orders and 32,920 of spend at today's rates (32,214 to 33,891 with TikTok's range), against 23,900 now.",
    "A Meta test for a 15% lift needs 42,515 clicks, about 35,012 and 83 days at today's budget, so it can't give an answer; in 28 days the budget can detect a lift of 26.5% or more."
  ],
